1
00:01:28,284 --> 00:01:34,089
HER FIRST LOVE WAS... RYOTSU?

2
00:01:35,057 --> 00:01:35,658
"REPORT"

3
00:01:38,527 --> 00:01:40,829
&lt;i&gt;Chief Ohara, would you like some tea?&lt;/i&gt;

4
00:01:42,498 --> 00:01:43,432
&lt;i&gt;Oh, thanks.&lt;/i&gt;

5
00:01:43,899 --> 00:01:47,136
&lt;i&gt;You should take it easy.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;It's not good for your health.&lt;/i&gt;

6
00:01:47,469 --> 00:01:51,240
&lt;i&gt;No, well, you see,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;I have to finish this paperwork today.&lt;/i&gt;

7
00:01:51,540 --> 00:01:54,376
&lt;i&gt;I see. Well, please don't&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;push yourself too hard.&lt;/i&gt;

8
00:01:54,710 --> 00:01:56,512
&lt;i&gt;Oh, thank you, Ms. Asada.&lt;/i&gt;

9
00:01:56,712 --> 00:02:00,182
&lt;i&gt;You don't need to call me that.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;You can just call me Yuko.&lt;/i&gt;

10
00:02:00,482 --> 00:02:03,919
&lt;i&gt;Oh, all right... Yu...&lt;/i&gt;

11
00:02:04,119 --> 00:02:05,187
&lt;i&gt;Yu.... ko.&lt;/i&gt;

12
00:02:05,554 --> 00:02:06,455
Yuko...

13
00:02:06,655 --> 00:02:11,193
-Hey, officer! Officer, are you listening? -Huh?

14
00:02:11,627 --> 00:02:14,630
Which way to the bus stop at Bakuro-Yokoyama Station?

15
00:02:14,830 --> 00:02:17,733
Oh, just keep following this road...

16
00:02:17,966 --> 00:02:18,967
See? Was that hard?

17
00:02:29,678 --> 00:02:33,282
Customers wishing to buy Yuko Asada's photo book that came out today,

18
00:02:33,482 --> 00:02:36,585
please line up here to make your purchase.

19
00:02:37,152 --> 00:02:40,823
Please, no pushing, and please form two lines.

20
00:02:41,156 --> 00:02:43,192
Now, these are limited edition.

21
00:02:43,392 --> 00:02:46,695
While we have plenty of stock, once they're gone, that's it.

22
00:02:46,895 --> 00:02:48,364
-Thank you. -My goodness.

23
00:02:49,331 --> 00:02:52,334
Yes, sir. Yes, I'll make sure I get it.

24
00:02:52,534 --> 00:02:53,202
Move!

25
00:02:57,373 --> 00:03:00,209
No, I can't. Not while I'm on duty.

26
00:03:00,542 --> 00:03:04,747
But...

27
00:03:04,980 --> 00:03:07,249
Secure your place in line quickly.

28
00:03:13,856 --> 00:03:15,791
This is the end of the line.

29
00:03:16,024 --> 00:03:17,860
Line up here for Yuko Asada's book.

30
00:03:18,060 --> 00:03:20,696
I hope they'll still have some left.

31
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:30,773
Thank you. Thank you.

32
00:03:32,474 --> 00:03:35,911
Thank you.

33
00:03:39,281 --> 00:03:42,384
Who's that making all that ruckus?

34
00:03:42,584 --> 00:03:44,787
Thank you. Thank you.

35
00:03:45,020 --> 00:03:46,188
Mine!

36
00:03:46,655 --> 00:03:47,556
Chief?

37
00:03:47,756 --> 00:03:49,291
Oh, what a relief!

38
00:03:49,491 --> 00:03:52,461
I'll take one! No, two! One to keep pristine!

39
00:03:52,928 --> 00:03:54,129
Thank you.

40
00:03:54,496 --> 00:03:56,098
Hooray!

41
00:03:56,431 --> 00:03:58,300
I'm so happy!

42
00:03:59,201 --> 00:04:00,102
Chief!

43
00:04:02,838 --> 00:04:05,607
Gah! Ryotsu, why are you here?

44
00:04:05,808 --> 00:04:07,576
You can't fool me, Chief.

45
00:04:07,776 --> 00:04:09,978
I saw it with my own eyes.

46
00:04:10,212 --> 00:04:13,248
To think... The chief, of all people, slacking off.

47
00:04:13,448 --> 00:04:16,919
And what about you? What's that in your hand?

48
00:04:17,453 --> 00:04:21,857
I'm out here looking for shoplifters. Something just happened to catch my eye.

49
00:04:22,090 --> 00:04:23,325
You? On patrol?

50
00:04:23,525 --> 00:04:25,327
All right, no need for a fuss.

51
00:04:25,527 --> 00:04:27,930
Now, let me have a look at yours too.

52
00:04:28,130 --> 00:04:30,466
Hey, give that back! Hey!

53
00:04:30,699 --> 00:04:31,633
Huh?

54
00:04:32,267 --> 00:04:33,469
What kinda book is this?

55
00:04:34,269 --> 00:04:36,171
It's not a nudie book?

56
00:04:36,672 --> 00:04:39,975
Of course not. Yuko Asada would never!

57
00:04:43,245 --> 00:04:46,248
She's really pretty. I'd imagine women want to be her.

58
00:04:46,448 --> 00:04:48,183
She does command your gaze.

59
00:04:48,417 --> 00:04:53,288
She's the only Japanese actress who's made it big worldwide.

60
00:04:53,722 --> 00:04:55,724
Oh, yes. You're right.

61
00:04:56,358 --> 00:04:59,127
Let me see. I didn't get a good look before.

62
00:04:59,328 --> 00:05:02,331
Watch it, Ryotsu. Don't be so rough.

63
00:05:02,531 --> 00:05:06,335
Pft... Chief. Who'd have thought your taste in women would be so basic?

64
00:05:06,535 --> 00:05:10,005
If everyone likes her, that means she has no personality...

65
00:05:11,707 --> 00:05:15,110
Get your snotty face away. And don't crease it!

66
00:05:15,310 --> 00:05:19,715
No, hold on a minute. I've seen this actress somewhere before.

67
00:05:20,048 --> 00:05:21,550
What? Yuko Asada?

68
00:05:21,984 --> 00:05:26,054
You're an idiot. You think everyone on TV is your friend.

69
00:05:26,655 --> 00:05:31,159
No, this is different. I'm sure I've seen her somewhere before.

70
00:05:32,461 --> 00:05:34,997
-What's that? -It's a TV station car.

71
00:05:35,564 --> 00:05:38,000
Hey! Is there a Ryotsu in the house? Kan-chan?

72
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:39,668
Yes, but...

73
00:05:40,068 --> 00:05:41,703
What have you done this time?

74
00:05:41,904 --> 00:05:43,672
I haven't done anything!

75
00:05:43,939 --> 00:05:45,507
Are you Kan-chan?

76
00:05:45,707 --> 00:05:47,910
Hmm... Yep, you've got pizzazz!

77
00:05:48,143 --> 00:05:51,246
And what a mug! Your face was made for TV!

78
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:52,214
Good!

79
00:05:52,414 --> 00:05:53,916
What do you mean, TV?

80
00:05:54,416 --> 00:05:59,555
I'm Mizusawa. A director at KTV.

81
00:05:59,755 --> 00:06:03,926
I've come to ask Kan-chan here to appear on our show.

82
00:06:04,159 --> 00:06:05,727
You want this turkey on TV?

83
00:06:05,928 --> 00:06:08,764
You bet! You're a smooth operator, right, Kan-chan?

84
00:06:09,364 --> 00:06:12,601
She'll be thrilled to know her first love has her photo album.

85
00:06:12,801 --> 00:06:14,169
Huh? Who?

86
00:06:14,570 --> 00:06:15,971
You silly billy.

87
00:06:16,204 --> 00:06:20,342
You're her first crush. The one and only Yuko Asada's first love.

88
00:06:20,642 --> 00:06:23,345
Ryotsu is Yuko Asada's first love?

89
00:06:23,612 --> 00:06:24,880
What?!

90
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:26,882
Are you sure about that?

91
00:06:27,182 --> 00:06:31,053
Yes, it must be a mistake! I refuse to believe otherwise!

92
00:06:31,453 --> 00:06:34,523
KTV doesn't miss a beat with this sort of thing.

93
00:06:35,290 --> 00:06:38,293
We have proof, Kan-chan. Lookie here!

94
00:06:39,127 --> 00:06:40,462
Hey, that's me!

95
00:06:41,196 --> 00:06:46,201
Yuko's mom picked you out from her elementary school photo album.

96
00:06:46,401 --> 00:06:49,404
You've been camera-ready ever since you were a kid.

97
00:06:49,605 --> 00:06:52,107
This is from that field trip.

98
00:06:52,307 --> 00:06:53,742
Oh, I remember now!

99
00:06:53,942 --> 00:06:58,113
There was this girl with big eyes at the kimono shop behind the school.

100
00:06:58,413 --> 00:07:02,384
That's her! That little girl is now the current sensation, Yuko Asada!

101
00:07:02,918 --> 00:07:05,954
So you really have met her before.

102
00:07:06,254 --> 00:07:08,590
Ryotsu... was...

103
00:07:09,691 --> 00:07:13,462
Well, well. I had no idea she liked me back then.

104
00:07:14,463 --> 00:07:16,865
&lt;i&gt;You had her heart all aflutter.&lt;/i&gt;

105
00:07:17,099 --> 00:07:19,034
&lt;i&gt;The little lady hid with bated breath&lt;/i&gt;

106
00:07:19,267 --> 00:07:21,637
&lt;i&gt;as she watched her beloved Kan-chan.&lt;/i&gt;

107
00:07:22,838 --> 00:07:25,440
-You lucky fella... -That's me!

108
00:07:25,707 --> 00:07:28,110
Yuko-san! My delicate, precious white lily!

109
00:07:28,310 --> 00:07:30,879
You fell for this caveman?!

110
00:07:31,246 --> 00:07:35,717
Impossible. Unbelievable. Say it isn't so!

111
00:07:36,485 --> 00:07:40,022
But I never even spoke to her.

112
00:07:40,255 --> 00:07:42,724
That's because it was a one-sided love.

113
00:07:42,958 --> 00:07:45,360
You see, we did some digging.

114
00:07:45,594 --> 00:07:48,430
You were a handsome athlete with long, sturdy legs?

115
00:07:48,630 --> 00:07:50,065
Long legs?

116
00:07:50,666 --> 00:07:52,868
Even "short" would be an understatement.

117
00:07:53,068 --> 00:07:55,504
Maybe it was just a trick of the eye?

118
00:07:55,837 --> 00:07:57,873
And you had a lovely nickname.

119
00:07:58,540 --> 00:08:01,343
Ryotsu, what was your nickname as a kid?

120
00:08:01,543 --> 00:08:04,446
I think it was "dung beetle."

121
00:08:05,180 --> 00:08:08,183
-Very fitting. -But not very "nice."

122
00:08:08,383 --> 00:08:09,618
Could you be mistaken?

123
00:08:10,619 --> 00:08:13,355
KTV never misses a beat!

124
00:08:13,822 --> 00:08:15,857
All right, this will settle it.

125
00:08:16,058 --> 00:08:19,227
What about the love letter in your locker on graduation day?

126
00:08:19,695 --> 00:08:21,830
Huh? A love letter in my locker?

127
00:08:22,030 --> 00:08:24,633
I don't remember anything nice like that.

128
00:08:24,833 --> 00:08:28,670
Of course you got it. Are you saying Yuko is a liar?

129
00:08:28,870 --> 00:08:31,840
Right. Try to remember, Ryotsu!

130
00:08:32,040 --> 00:08:35,210
Come on, remember! Remember! Remember! Come on!

131
00:08:35,410 --> 00:08:38,380
Hmm, now that you mention it, maybe I did.

132
00:08:38,580 --> 00:08:40,682
You did! You definitely did!

133
00:08:40,882 --> 00:08:43,385
Okay! Yes, I got a love letter!

134
00:08:43,585 --> 00:08:47,322
See? I told you we never miss a beat.

135
00:08:47,723 --> 00:08:50,092
&lt;i&gt;Yeah. I think I'm starting to remember.&lt;/i&gt;

136
00:08:50,325 --> 00:08:54,796
She left it between my shoes. And I think the envelope was... pink?

137
00:08:55,230 --> 00:08:57,065
Pink! Bingo!

138
00:08:57,399 --> 00:08:58,700
I knew it!

139
00:08:58,900 --> 00:09:00,869
Yeah, I'm right!

140
00:09:01,803 --> 00:09:04,106
I'm Yuko Asada's first love!

141
00:09:04,406 --> 00:09:05,774
Then that settles it.

142
00:09:06,241 --> 00:09:08,710
So you'll be waiting for my call, yeah?

143
00:09:08,910 --> 00:09:09,945
Peace out!

144
00:09:11,246 --> 00:09:12,881
That's amazing, Ryo-chan.

145
00:09:13,081 --> 00:09:16,518
We were so close we called each other "Kan-chan" and "Yuurin."

146
00:09:16,718 --> 00:09:18,453
You called her "Yuurin"?

147
00:09:18,887 --> 00:09:20,956
Stranger things have happened...

148
00:09:21,556 --> 00:09:24,793
All right, Ryotsu. I've got a favor to ask you.

149
00:09:24,993 --> 00:09:26,695
A favor? What is it?

150
00:09:26,895 --> 00:09:31,399
When you see Yuko-san, could you get her to sign my photo book?

151
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:34,970
"To Ohara-san with love," yeah? It'll be a family heirloom, okay?

152
00:09:35,537 --> 00:09:40,375
That's a bold ask, even coming from her first love.

153
00:09:40,575 --> 00:09:42,277
But there must be some way?

154
00:09:42,611 --> 00:09:45,280
Well, if you insist...

155
00:09:45,614 --> 00:09:46,581
Oh, you will?

156
00:09:46,915 --> 00:09:51,553
If you copy what I'm about to do, I'll make it happen.

157
00:09:51,753 --> 00:09:56,758
I used to do this as a kid, and it got the whole assembly laughing.

158
00:09:57,125 --> 00:09:58,326
What is it?

159
00:09:58,560 --> 00:10:02,330
Knowing Ryo-chan, it's got to be something vulgar.

160
00:10:02,597 --> 00:10:04,266
Ugh, you're right.

161
00:10:04,633 --> 00:10:07,335
Well, if you don't want to, that's fine.

162
00:10:07,936 --> 00:10:12,774
I'll bet Yuurin loved my little joke.

163
00:10:12,974 --> 00:10:16,845
Fine. If I do this gag, you'll get her autograph, right?

164
00:10:17,179 --> 00:10:19,181
Yup. I give you my word as a man.

165
00:10:19,414 --> 00:10:22,651
In fact, I'll do you one better. I'll let you come with me.

166
00:10:22,851 --> 00:10:24,820
Then you can even shake her hand.

167
00:10:25,020 --> 00:10:26,321
Shake her hand?

168
00:10:27,189 --> 00:10:28,456
&lt;i&gt;Hello there.&lt;/i&gt;

169
00:10:28,757 --> 00:10:31,893
All right, I'll do it! What do I do first?

170
00:10:32,327 --> 00:10:33,461
First...

171
00:10:33,795 --> 00:10:35,530
Stick your fingers in your nose!

172
00:10:37,232 --> 00:10:39,034
What's wrong? Go on then!

173
00:10:42,037 --> 00:10:42,771
There!

174
00:10:43,238 --> 00:10:44,072
Chief!

175
00:10:44,306 --> 00:10:45,774
-He's doing it. -Oh my.

176
00:10:46,308 --> 00:10:51,246
Apparapara Biroon!

177
00:10:51,847 --> 00:10:53,882
Well, Ryotsu? I've done my part.

178
00:10:54,249 --> 00:10:56,885
Forget it if you're not even serious.

179
00:10:57,652 --> 00:10:59,654
What? What did I do wrong?

180
00:11:00,088 --> 00:11:02,157
Where was the moon?

181
00:11:02,357 --> 00:11:03,858
M-Moon?

182
00:11:04,459 --> 00:11:07,329
You wanna see Yuko Asada in the flesh?

183
00:11:07,529 --> 00:11:09,331
Then show me those cheeks.

184
00:11:09,864 --> 00:11:10,999
Fine.

185
00:11:11,199 --> 00:11:15,237
Apparapara Biroon!

186
00:11:15,570 --> 00:11:18,106
Heh, aren't you ashamed of yourself?

187
00:11:18,340 --> 00:11:19,407
What?

188
00:11:19,641 --> 00:11:21,509
Heh, just kidding.

189
00:11:21,710 --> 00:11:27,415
Okay, leave it with me. I'm Yuko Asada's first love!

190
00:11:30,218 --> 00:11:32,254
All right, time to go.

191
00:11:32,487 --> 00:11:33,888
Ahem, Ohara-kun?

192
00:11:34,089 --> 00:11:35,023
Huh?

193
00:11:37,025 --> 00:11:38,093
Oh, yes. Of course.

194
00:11:40,095 --> 00:11:41,763
Cheers, bud.

195
00:11:43,932 --> 00:11:48,203
Ryo-chan's got the chief acting like his assistant.

196
00:11:48,403 --> 00:11:52,374
Well, he is indebted. Ryotsu is his ticket to meeting his idol.

197
00:11:58,580 --> 00:12:00,415
Oh, there's the TV station.

198
00:12:00,615 --> 00:12:01,850
Look, Ryotsu.

199
00:12:05,887 --> 00:12:07,622
TV stations are huge, huh?

200
00:12:07,856 --> 00:12:08,857
Hey, Ryotsu.

201
00:12:09,057 --> 00:12:10,325
Don't you worry.

202
00:12:11,226 --> 00:12:14,396
-Director Mizusawa please, doll. -Huh?

203
00:12:14,596 --> 00:12:15,597
Hey, Kan-chan.

204
00:12:16,097 --> 00:12:17,265
You finally made it.

205
00:12:17,599 --> 00:12:19,401
Hey, Mizusawa-chan!

206
00:12:19,601 --> 00:12:20,435
Oh, look!

207
00:12:20,635 --> 00:12:22,003
Omutaku from SMOP.

208
00:12:22,237 --> 00:12:23,471
Updown!

209
00:12:23,705 --> 00:12:24,472
Ah!

210
00:12:24,906 --> 00:12:27,442
Chief, Chief! That's Namie Omuro.

211
00:12:27,642 --> 00:12:30,879
What? A tsunami of omelets?

212
00:12:31,079 --> 00:12:35,483
Ugh, Chief. You just don't get it. Guess it's my thrill alone.

213
00:12:36,084 --> 00:12:38,486
The only one I care about is Yuko Asada.

214
00:12:38,954 --> 00:12:42,624
And because I'm her first love, you get to meet her.

215
00:12:42,824 --> 00:12:44,959
You'd better remember this, Chief.

216
00:12:45,593 --> 00:12:46,494
I know, I know.

217
00:12:46,795 --> 00:12:48,830
Kan-chan, looking sharp as always.

218
00:12:49,030 --> 00:12:51,466
Hehe, it's just the usual. Take it easy.

219
00:12:51,666 --> 00:12:53,768
Is this Yuurin? Yuurin!

220
00:12:53,969 --> 00:12:55,503
That's a live broadcast!

221
00:13:09,584 --> 00:13:11,286
"RYOTSU-SAMA'S DRESSING ROOM"

222
00:13:11,853 --> 00:13:13,188
Filming starts at 3 p.m.

223
00:13:13,388 --> 00:13:16,491
Just be patient and wait here, okay?

224
00:13:16,858 --> 00:13:19,527
Don't keep the big actress waiting too long.

225
00:13:19,761 --> 00:13:21,763
On it. Toodles!

226
00:13:22,697 --> 00:13:25,233
Jeez, you'd think he'd mention the stale tea.

227
00:13:25,467 --> 00:13:27,202
And no lunch to boot?

228
00:13:27,402 --> 00:13:32,941
Maitsuru do good tonkatsu, or even Tsudaya do good seaweed sets.

229
00:13:33,308 --> 00:13:34,876
Huh? What's wrong, Chief?

230
00:13:35,210 --> 00:13:36,878
I need to use the restroom.

231
00:13:37,612 --> 00:13:40,415
Oh, Chief. There's no need to be so tense.

232
00:13:40,648 --> 00:13:41,683
I'll wet myself!

233
00:13:43,184 --> 00:13:44,686
Phew. That feels better.

234
00:13:44,886 --> 00:13:47,856
Jeez, you can handle a whizz on your own next time.

235
00:13:48,056 --> 00:13:51,159
I just can't handle being on my own, you know?

236
00:13:51,359 --> 00:13:53,661
Tch, amateurs. Such a pain.

237
00:13:53,862 --> 00:13:55,096
-Right... -Now...

238
00:13:55,330 --> 00:13:56,398
-Which... -Way...

239
00:14:01,069 --> 00:14:03,905
Huh? Which way did we come from?

240
00:14:04,372 --> 00:14:05,173
Well, whatever.

241
00:14:05,373 --> 00:14:07,909
Hey, Ryotsu. Wasn't it this way?

242
00:14:08,643 --> 00:14:11,579
Don't be such a worry wart. You're with me, remember?

243
00:14:11,813 --> 00:14:13,548
Huh? Was this it?

244
00:14:15,183 --> 00:14:16,251
Time for make up!

245
00:14:17,085 --> 00:14:18,887
-Allow me. -Um...

246
00:14:21,890 --> 00:14:23,892
Hey! I'm the one going on TV!

247
00:14:26,361 --> 00:14:27,662
Wrong room, huh?

248
00:14:27,862 --> 00:14:29,130
Get it together, Ryotsu.

249
00:14:29,364 --> 00:14:30,665
I'm counting on you.

250
00:14:31,199 --> 00:14:34,269
We're fine. We just need to be at the studio on time.

251
00:14:34,469 --> 00:14:36,738
It'll be your head if you mess up again!

252
00:14:36,938 --> 00:14:38,573
Huh? You sure about that?

253
00:14:38,773 --> 00:14:41,309
Do you not want to meet Yuko Asada after all?

254
00:14:41,709 --> 00:14:42,777
No, I was kidding!

255
00:14:43,011 --> 00:14:45,680
It's funny, right? Don't say that, please.

256
00:14:45,880 --> 00:14:47,148
Then we're in agreement.

257
00:14:47,382 --> 00:14:49,484
Now shut up and follow me.

258
00:14:49,717 --> 00:14:51,686
-Ryotsu...! -Did I hear something?

259
00:14:51,886 --> 00:14:53,321
Nothing...

260
00:14:53,555 --> 00:14:54,789
"STUDIO 1"

261
00:15:01,930 --> 00:15:03,231
Are we allowed in here?

262
00:15:03,431 --> 00:15:04,466
No idea.

263
00:15:07,735 --> 00:15:09,504
Hey, Chief. We're on camera.

264
00:15:12,307 --> 00:15:13,308
Is it this camera?

265
00:15:14,876 --> 00:15:15,877
Who's that?

266
00:15:18,279 --> 00:15:20,048
Which one is live?

267
00:15:20,248 --> 00:15:22,050
Is it this one? This one? Here?

268
00:15:23,918 --> 00:15:25,286
Get them out of there!

269
00:15:25,620 --> 00:15:27,889
Chief, Chief! Look, I'm on camera!

270
00:15:28,423 --> 00:15:30,258
I don't know you.

271
00:15:30,458 --> 00:15:32,260
-What are you doing? -Hold it! Hey!

272
00:15:33,361 --> 00:15:35,063
No, I don't know this man—

273
00:15:35,830 --> 00:15:37,432
Don't you know who I am?

274
00:15:37,632 --> 00:15:39,901
I'm Yuko Asada's first love!

275
00:15:41,503 --> 00:15:43,838
Why'd you drag me into this?

276
00:15:55,016 --> 00:15:57,018
Jeez, how very rude.

277
00:15:57,218 --> 00:15:58,019
Hmm?

278
00:15:58,553 --> 00:16:00,321
Something smells delicious.

279
00:16:00,522 --> 00:16:01,789
"STUDIO 2"

280
00:16:02,357 --> 00:16:06,294
Hello. I'm Kankichi Ryotsu, Yuko Asada's first love.

281
00:16:07,128 --> 00:16:08,530
Is anyone here?

282
00:16:09,164 --> 00:16:10,398
Hey! Huh?

283
00:16:10,765 --> 00:16:11,533
Oh?

284
00:16:11,766 --> 00:16:13,668
Why is there food here?

285
00:16:13,868 --> 00:16:15,670
Maybe it's for a show?

286
00:16:16,871 --> 00:16:20,842
This is perfect. I was getting hungry. Let's eat it.

287
00:16:21,142 --> 00:16:22,477
I don't think we should.

288
00:16:22,677 --> 00:16:24,812
It's delicious! Chief, have some.

289
00:16:25,013 --> 00:16:26,247
But...

290
00:16:30,585 --> 00:16:35,590
First up, for our famous Chinese dishes, we have "The Peking Man of Cooking."

291
00:16:35,823 --> 00:16:37,525
Let us reveal today's dishes!

292
00:16:44,866 --> 00:16:46,067
You idiots!

293
00:16:46,534 --> 00:16:48,703
Hey! We weren't done eating yet!

294
00:16:48,903 --> 00:16:50,805
Ryotsu, we're running out of time.

295
00:16:51,005 --> 00:16:52,273
I know, I know!

296
00:16:52,507 --> 00:16:53,808
"STUDIO 3"

297
00:16:55,977 --> 00:17:01,082
Amazing! It's Ivan Hibanavich, the human flamethrower from Russia!

298
00:17:01,616 --> 00:17:03,418
Ryotsu, is this the right place?

299
00:17:03,618 --> 00:17:05,019
Yeah, it's gotta be.

300
00:17:05,219 --> 00:17:10,692
Hey, the set looks like just plywood from the back.

301
00:17:25,239 --> 00:17:27,609
Why is it always me?

302
00:17:30,245 --> 00:17:31,179
Damn you, Ryotsu!

303
00:17:31,379 --> 00:17:33,014
Ah! There you are.

304
00:17:33,214 --> 00:17:35,783
What are you doing? The show's about to start!

305
00:17:36,117 --> 00:17:37,585
-Ah, okay! -Right.

306
00:17:37,785 --> 00:17:39,120
"KAMEARI PARK POLICE STATION"

307
00:17:39,487 --> 00:17:40,922
It's about to start.

308
00:17:41,122 --> 00:17:42,890
Will Ryo-chan be okay?

309
00:17:43,091 --> 00:17:45,093
Do you think we'll see the chief?

310
00:17:45,293 --> 00:17:47,428
"STUDIO 5"

311
00:17:49,564 --> 00:17:52,033
Oh, my heart is pounding.

312
00:17:54,602 --> 00:17:58,640
Hello, everyone. It's time for "3 O'clock Guy."

313
00:17:59,207 --> 00:18:04,479
Today's guest is Yuko Asada, one of Japan's most popular actresses.

314
00:18:05,046 --> 00:18:07,949
-Hello. I'm Yuko Asada. -She really is stunning.

315
00:18:08,249 --> 00:18:09,784
Even more so up close...

316
00:18:14,689 --> 00:18:16,457
She's dazzling!

317
00:18:17,792 --> 00:18:21,329
Give her this bouquet when you go out to meet her.

318
00:18:21,529 --> 00:18:22,463
Got it?

319
00:18:22,897 --> 00:18:28,336
Got it. Then I get her to talk about how cool she thought I was as a kid, yeah?

320
00:18:28,536 --> 00:18:30,471
Got it, got it. Leave it with me.

321
00:18:30,838 --> 00:18:35,476
Now, it's time for the much-anticipated "Memorable Reunion" segment!

322
00:18:36,010 --> 00:18:37,111
This is it.

323
00:18:38,913 --> 00:18:40,648
Okay, Asada-san. Are you ready?

324
00:18:40,848 --> 00:18:42,517
Oh, I'm getting nervous.

325
00:18:42,717 --> 00:18:45,853
First, the silhouette quiz. Recognize this man?

326
00:18:49,257 --> 00:18:51,559
Sorry, this isn't really enough to go by.

327
00:18:52,260 --> 00:18:56,097
&lt;i&gt;Well, understandable.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Not like I'm a school kid anymore.&lt;/i&gt;

328
00:18:56,698 --> 00:19:00,368
Now we'll have the mystery man call you by your old nickname. Ready?

329
00:19:00,568 --> 00:19:02,003
If you will!

330
00:19:02,203 --> 00:19:03,204
Yuurin.

331
00:19:03,671 --> 00:19:04,972
I still don't know.

332
00:19:07,275 --> 00:19:10,378
She'll be head over heels when she finally realizes.

333
00:19:11,846 --> 00:19:14,816
&lt;i&gt;Oh! It's... Kan-chan!&lt;/i&gt;

334
00:19:15,550 --> 00:19:17,885
&lt;i&gt;Yuurin!&lt;/i&gt;

335
00:19:20,388 --> 00:19:23,057
&lt;i&gt;"Yuurin!" This is gonna be great.&lt;/i&gt;

336
00:19:23,591 --> 00:19:26,594
&lt;i&gt;What if she asks me to marry her?&lt;/i&gt;

337
00:19:27,128 --> 00:19:29,297
All right, I'll give you a big hint.

338
00:19:29,497 --> 00:19:31,899
His last name starts with an "R".

339
00:19:32,133 --> 00:19:33,568
An "R"?

340
00:19:34,535 --> 00:19:38,039
Ah, she's a beauty even through her confusion.

341
00:19:38,573 --> 00:19:41,075
All right, here's another big hint.

342
00:19:41,309 --> 00:19:42,844
His first name is "Kankichi"!

343
00:19:43,444 --> 00:19:45,413
Kankichi-san?

344
00:19:46,013 --> 00:19:47,749
&lt;i&gt;Still don't remember?&lt;/i&gt;

345
00:19:47,982 --> 00:19:50,418
&lt;i&gt;Ugh, just say my full name.&lt;/i&gt;

346
00:19:50,918 --> 00:19:54,622
Hey, what's going on, Mizusawa-chan? Sort it out.

347
00:19:55,390 --> 00:19:56,758
It's fine. I got this.

348
00:19:56,991 --> 00:19:59,527
I guess even the best of us stumble at times.

349
00:19:59,894 --> 00:20:03,398
Shall we just reveal his full name? His name is...

350
00:20:05,767 --> 00:20:08,636
Kankichi Ryotsu!

351
00:20:10,571 --> 00:20:11,205
Huh?

352
00:20:11,572 --> 00:20:13,207
Kankichi Ryotsu.

353
00:20:14,208 --> 00:20:16,377
Kankichi Ryotsu?

354
00:20:17,211 --> 00:20:19,113
Yes, Kankichi Ryotsu!

355
00:20:20,481 --> 00:20:21,349
Who is that?

356
00:20:23,551 --> 00:20:26,087
-I have a bad feeling about this. -Yeah.

357
00:20:26,821 --> 00:20:31,492
She may never forget a line, but I guess she can forget a name.

358
00:20:31,726 --> 00:20:34,095
Well, he is from your childhood days.

359
00:20:34,295 --> 00:20:38,366
Okay, since we're having some trouble, let's just have him come on out!

360
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:41,836
&lt;i&gt;She may not recall my name,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;but she should know my face.&lt;/i&gt;

361
00:20:43,771 --> 00:20:46,140
Come on out, Kankichi Ryotsu!

362
00:20:50,778 --> 00:20:52,447
Yuurin!

363
00:20:52,947 --> 00:20:54,515
-Who is this man? -Eh?!

364
00:20:55,416 --> 00:20:56,784
Ah, uh, um...

365
00:20:57,218 --> 00:20:58,286
What's going on?

366
00:20:58,853 --> 00:21:02,790
His nickname was "dung beetle." Come on, you must remember!

367
00:21:02,990 --> 00:21:03,958
No...

368
00:21:04,959 --> 00:21:05,693
No?

369
00:21:06,127 --> 00:21:07,328
What is going on here?

370
00:21:07,528 --> 00:21:10,231
Show her the photo. And the love letter.

371
00:21:10,665 --> 00:21:15,102
Well, it has been over twenty years. Can't be easy remembering that long ago...

372
00:21:15,303 --> 00:21:16,003
Oh?

373
00:21:16,537 --> 00:21:19,607
Oh, how could I forget?

374
00:21:19,807 --> 00:21:22,944
Asada-san, remember the love letter in the locker?

375
00:21:23,611 --> 00:21:26,647
Love letter? In a locker? Now that you mention it...

376
00:21:27,014 --> 00:21:28,816
It was this guy.

377
00:21:29,016 --> 00:21:31,352
A childhood photo is sure to jog your memory.

378
00:21:32,820 --> 00:21:33,621
Here he is.

379
00:21:34,455 --> 00:21:36,624
The recipient of your letter. It's Ryotsu.

380
00:21:37,024 --> 00:21:38,526
-Huh? -Never mind that.

381
00:21:39,026 --> 00:21:41,896
I've got a gag that'll help you remember.

382
00:21:42,129 --> 00:21:42,864
Huh? A joke?

383
00:21:43,197 --> 00:21:46,167
Remember? I was the funniest guy in school.

384
00:21:46,367 --> 00:21:49,837
I made the entire assembly laugh with this pose!

385
00:21:50,137 --> 00:21:52,173
Okay, let's see it. Go ahead!

386
00:21:52,507 --> 00:21:53,207
Ahem!

387
00:21:56,377 --> 00:21:58,579
Apparapara Biroon!

388
00:21:58,813 --> 00:22:00,548
Oh! I remember now!

389
00:22:00,915 --> 00:22:04,185
Hooray! A touching reunion!

390
00:22:08,823 --> 00:22:09,524
I knew it!

391
00:22:09,724 --> 00:22:12,226
That's the boy who scribbled on my gym uniform,

392
00:22:12,560 --> 00:22:15,029
and was always peeping into the girl's bathroom!

393
00:22:15,229 --> 00:22:16,898
It's Kankichi Ryotsu!

394
00:22:19,367 --> 00:22:21,402
You giant numbskull!

395
00:22:21,736 --> 00:22:25,072
But your mother pointed out your first love from this photo.

396
00:22:25,306 --> 00:22:28,776
I didn't give him a love letter. I gave it to this boy!

397
00:22:30,711 --> 00:22:34,215
You blundering oaf! How did you think he was her first love?

398
00:22:34,415 --> 00:22:35,850
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

399
00:22:36,217 --> 00:22:38,853
This guy was the most vulgar person at school.

400
00:22:39,153 --> 00:22:41,022
Kankichi Ryotsu!

401
00:22:41,689 --> 00:22:47,762
&lt;i&gt;Kankichi Ryotsu!&lt;/i&gt;

402
00:22:52,500 --> 00:22:54,435
Is this on national TV?

403
00:22:55,202 --> 00:22:58,339
You moron!

404
00:23:03,744 --> 00:23:06,247
Apparapara Biroon!

405
00:23:06,647 --> 00:23:08,749
Ryotsu. You call that a gag?

406
00:23:08,950 --> 00:23:10,818
Put your back into it!

407
00:23:11,052 --> 00:23:12,119
I am, I am!

408
00:23:12,353 --> 00:23:14,121
Haven't I done enough already?

409
00:23:14,822 --> 00:23:18,993
No way. This is payback for messing up my Yuko Asada's show!

410
00:23:19,226 --> 00:23:23,297
Ready, everyone? Feel free to vent all your pent-up anger.

411
00:23:23,531 --> 00:23:25,199
We will.

412
00:23:27,201 --> 00:23:29,070
Chief!

413
00:23:30,571 --> 00:23:34,141
Apparapara Biroon!

414
00:23:34,942 --> 00:23:36,911
Do it properly, Ryotsu.

415
00:23:38,279 --> 00:23:39,847
Hey! Thanks for the other day.

416
00:23:40,314 --> 00:23:41,482
What? Not you!

417
00:23:41,816 --> 00:23:46,120
As it turns out, our ratings have never been higher.

418
00:23:46,320 --> 00:23:48,589
What can I say? That's live TV for ya.

419
00:23:48,789 --> 00:23:51,625
So, I was thinking... What if we had you as a regular?

420
00:23:51,826 --> 00:23:54,962
We could have a "Who's That?" segment every single day!

421
00:23:55,162 --> 00:23:56,497
No way! I refuse!

422
00:23:57,331 --> 00:24:00,835
I am never going on TV ever again!
